23rn|v|To press between two bodies; to press together closely; to compress; often, to compress so as to expel juice, moisture, etc.; as, to squeeze an orange with the fingers; to squeeze the hand in friendship. ; Fig.: To oppress with hardships, burdens, or taxes; to harass; to crush. ; To force, or cause to pass, by compression; often with out, through, etc.; as, to squeeze water through felt. ; To press; to urge one's way, or to pass, by pressing; to crowd; -- often with through, into, etc.; as, to squeeze hard to get through a crowd.	o:8y1,96,6;s56,36,4~8y1,96,6;s56,36,4	d:28oo,11,6~28oo,11,6	D:29qk,33,9;1jly,13,5~29qk,33,9;1jly,13,5
